all.checked_ok:
I found no path by which a held-out label, or anything derived from one, reaches a block-A fit, its inner λ choice, the inner B1 refit, or a prediction. What I checked:

(1) Every input of SA._situations and SA.fit_slot is outer-training only:
- training cells are the inner blocks' validation records plus the orphans (RF.training_cells), filtered by wmap over outer train_index;
- Y is indexed only at those cells;
- cell weights use groups and n_obs of outer-train cells;
- DOPT_Q is either the cached nested sequence or recomputed from blk['cov'] (fitted on itr);
- UNIFORM is label-free; RANDOM masks are seeded by cell_id;
- inner-fit rows are restricted to blk['train_index'] (design mask re-applied); validation rows are restricted to blk['val_index'] under DOPT_Q only.

(2) Empirical check on BP 155921 fold 2, the orphan fold (training side only, no scoring):
- slot situations equal B1's bit for bit (Xg, r, w), outer and in each of the 3 inner blocks;
- SA._beta on the slot's outer rows reproduces b1['coef'] exactly;
- 0 validation cells in any inner fit; 0 test cells in any situation.
So B1 is refitted on inner-train rows inside each block (β only; see A-NEST-1), and the outer B1 coefficient enters only the final refit target.

(3) predict_levels reads only obs.y_masked (reads only, per g21 observe), the cell's metals, the fitted b1, coef and spec, and the class. Read metals stay exact; λ = ∞ returns B1 bit for bit, because it is the same b1 object plus 0.0.

(4) Donor class is a pure function of the extractant SMILES:
- DGA SMARTS, plus the gen19 InChIKey→mechanism map;
- mechanism comes from gen19's fixed structural FAMILY_MECHANISM table, not from data;
- 0 InChIKeys in the CSV have conflicting mechanisms;
- the same function serves training records and test cells (cell['extractant'] comes from cell_view = frame.extractant).

(5) The S21 map uses only chemotype, extractant and donor class from bench.frame. One global map is stored in the fit and used for both training and test. Extractant→chemotype is a function (0 extractants span two chemotypes), so the map is well defined and has no KeyError path. Fit poisoning keeps those columns, so the map is identical on the poisoned bench.

(6) In-process fit poisoning (no files written) on BPG 155921/2 and BPG 104729/0: B1, S01, S02, S04 draw 0 and S21:S01 draw 2 are all deep_equal identical. The fitted slot dict holds only plain data (spec with a perm ndarray, coef, inner_scores keyed by str, b1, columns, class_map). The cls_of lambda is not stored, so the dicts pickle cleanly and deep_equal compares them meaningfully.

(7) The intervention covers the slot columns: factory → RG.get(cid, scrambled bench) rebuilds the _slot_method closures, which capture no bench and read only block['fitted']. They are compared column by column with B0, B1 and B2.

(8) No reuse across folds:
- r4_run checkpoints are keyed by cid (with ':' removed), design, seal, seed and fold;
- RF._ORPHANS is keyed by (id(bench), design, seed, fold) and holds a strong reference to the bench, so ids cannot be reused;
- the lru_caches (shapes, donor_class, _mechanisms) are label-free;
- CF.INNER_CACHE_DIR is not used by slot configs;
- smoke writes nothing.

(9) The physics basis is pure physics (radius, f-count). The P2-P5 polynomials are label-free. None of the 5 permutations leaves Gd in place (seed 20261023 fixes only Nd). S04 and S21 rerun inner tuning per draw, as brief §8.6 requires.

(10) All 50 dev folds have at least 3 scored inner blocks, so the empty-folds tie-to-∞ path is unreachable. tests/test_slots_a.py: 6 passed.

Context, not a leakage issue: the S21 shuffle leaves sc009 (363 of its 375 cohort cells are DGA) at DGA in 4 of the 5 draws. Only 46–82 of the 229 C3 cells change class in those draws, and 181 in draw 20261125. The control therefore keeps most of the true assignment and is conservative, which matches the synthetic CHEM_D7 result (S21:S01 draws at about 48% of S01).

Disclosure for A1: checks (2) and (6) showed me fit-side outputs (λ, coefficients) for S01, S02, S04 d0 and S21:S01 d2 on BPG 155921/2 and BPG 104729/0. No outer metric was computed. These should be listed in A1's 'results seen', next to the technical smokes.

